    // Intro & research
    "Web cache deception is a vulnerability that enables an attacker to trick a web cache into storing sensitive, dynamic content. It's caused by discrepancies between how the cache server and origin server handle requests." => 'Web cache deception adalah kerentanan yang memungkinkan penyerang menipu web cache agar menyimpan konten dinamis sensitif akibat perbedaan tafsir permintaan antara server cache dan server asal.',
    "In a web cache deception attack, an attacker persuades a victim to visit a malicious URL, inducing the victim's browser to make an ambiguous request for sensitive content. The cache misinterprets this as a request for a static resource and stores the response. The attacker can then request the same URL to access the cached response, gaining unauthorized access to private information." => 'Penyerang memancing korban mengunjungi URL ambigu; server asal tetap mengembalikan data privat korban sementara cache mengiranya aset statis dan menyimpannya agar dapat diambil penyerang.',
    "It's important to distinguish web cache deception from web cache poisoning. While both exploit caching mechanisms, they do so in different ways:" => 'Penting untuk membedakan web cache deception dengan web cache poisoning:',
    'Web cache poisoning manipulates cache keys to inject malicious content into a cached response, which is then served to other users.' => 'Web cache poisoning memanipulasi cache key agar payload berbahaya masuk ke cache dan disajikan ke korban lain.',
    'Web cache deception exploits cache rules to trick the cache into storing sensitive or private content, which the attacker can then access.' => 'Web cache deception memanfaatkan aturan caching agar data privat milik korban ikut tersimpan di cache sehingga bisa diambil oleh penyerang.',
    'For more detailed information on web cache poisoning, refer to our [[A0]]Web cache poisoning[[/A0]] Academy topic.' => 'Penjelasan rinci web cache poisoning tersedia di topik [[A0]]Web cache poisoning[[/A0]].',
    'SecDevLab research' => 'Riset web cache deception',
    "SecDevLab has developed several deliberately vulnerable labs that you can use to safely practice what you've learned against realistic targets. Many of these labs are based on original research first presented at Black Hat USA 2024." => 'Lab dalam topik ini dibangun untuk menyimulasikan temuan nyata teknik manipulasi aturan web cache.',
    'For more details, please refer to the accompanying whitepaper: [[A0]]Gotta Cache \'em all: bending the rules of web cache exploitation[[/A0]].' => 'Simak publikasi terkait: [[A0]]Gotta Cache \'em all: bending the rules of web cache exploitation[[/A0]].',

    // Web caches mechanics
    'Web caches' => 'Web cache',
    "A web cache is a system that sits between the origin server and the user. When a client requests a static resource, the request is first directed to the cache. If the cache doesn't contain a copy of the resource (known as a cache miss), the request is forwarded to the origin server, which processes and responds to the request. The response is then sent to the cache before being sent to the user. The cache uses a preconfigured set of rules to determine whether to store the response." => 'Web cache berada di antara klien dan server asal. Saat terjadi cache miss, respons dari server asal dievaluasi berdasarkan aturan cache untuk menentukan apakah perlu disimpan.',
    'When a request for the same static resource is made in the future, the cache serves the stored copy of the response directly to the user (known as a cache hit).' => 'Jika terjadi permintaan berulang, cache langsung mengembalikan salinan tersebut (cache hit).',
    'Caching has become a common and crucial aspect of delivering web content, particularly with the widespread use of Content Delivery Networks (CDNs), which use caching to store copies of content on distributed servers all over the world. CDNs speed up delivery by serving content from the server closest to the user, reducing load times by minimizing the distance data travels.' => 'CDN menyebarkan salinan cache statis ke berbagai lokasi agar situs dimuat lebih cepat.',
    'Cache keys' => 'Cache key',
    "When the cache receives an HTTP request, it must decide whether there is a cached response that it can serve directly, or whether it has to forward the request to the origin server. The cache makes this decision by generating a 'cache key' from elements of the HTTP request. Typically, this includes the URL path and query parameters, but it can also include a variety of other elements like headers and content type." => 'Cache menentukan kesamaan permintaan menggunakan "cache key" yang biasanya disusun dari path URL, parameter query, dan header tertentu.',
    "If the incoming request's cache key matches that of a previous request, the cache considers them to be equivalent and serves a copy of the cached response." => 'Permintaan dengan cache key identik akan menerima respons yang sama dari cache.',
    'To learn how to manipulate cache keys to inject malicious content into the cache, see our [[A0]]Web cache poisoning[[/A0]] Academy topic.' => 'Cara memanipulasi cache key dibahas di topik [[A0]]Web cache poisoning[[/A0]].',
    'Cache rules' => 'Aturan cache',
    "Cache rules determine what can be cached and for how long. Cache rules are often set up to store static resources, which generally don't change frequently and are reused across multiple pages. Dynamic content is not cached as it's more likely to contain sensitive information, ensuring users get the latest data directly from the server." => 'Aturan cache umumnya dirancang hanya untuk menyimpan aset statis agar data dinamis sensitif tidak pernah disimpan.',
    "Web cache deception attacks exploit how cache rules are applied, so it's important to know about some different types of rules, particularly those based on defined strings in the URL path of the request. For example:" => 'Serangan web cache deception memanfaatkan cara pencocokan aturan cache di path URL, misalnya:',
    'Static file extension rules - These rules match the file extension of the requested resource, for example [[C0]] for stylesheets or [[C1]] for JavaScript files.' => 'Aturan ekstensi file statis, seperti akhiran [[C0]] atau [[C1]].',
    'Static directory rules - These rules match all URL paths that start with a specific prefix. These are often used to target specific directories that contain only static resources, for example [[C0]] or [[C1]].' => 'Aturan direktori statis, seperti prefiks [[C0]] atau [[C1]].',
    'File name rules - These rules match specific file names to target files that are universally required for web operations and change rarely, such as [[C0]] and [[C1]].' => 'Aturan nama file tertentu seperti [[C0]] dan [[C1]].',
    'Caches may also implement custom rules based on other criteria, such as URL parameters or dynamic analysis.' => 'Cache juga bisa memakai aturan kustom berdasarkan parameter URL atau analisis respons.',

    // Constructing attack
    'Constructing a web cache deception attack' => 'Menyusun serangan web cache deception',
    'Generally speaking, constructing a basic web cache deception attack involves the following steps:' => 'Tahapan umum penyusunan serangan web cache deception:',
    'Identify a target endpoint that returns a dynamic response containing sensitive information. Review responses in Burp, as some sensitive information may not be visible on the rendered page. Focus on endpoints that support the [[C0]], [[C1]], or [[C2]] methods as requests that alter the origin server\'s state are generally not cached.' => 'Cari endpoint sensitif yang merespons metode [[C0]], [[C1]], atau [[C2]].',
    'Identify a discrepancy in how the cache and origin server parse the URL path. This could be a discrepancy in how they:' => 'Temukan selisih parsing path URL antara server cache dan server asal dalam hal:',
    'Map URLs to resources.' => 'Pemetaan URL ke sumber daya.',
    'Process delimiter characters.' => 'Pemrosesan karakter delimiter.',
    'Normalize paths.' => 'Normalisasi path dan segmen titik.',
    'Craft a malicious URL that uses the discrepancy to trick the cache into storing a dynamic response. When the victim accesses the URL, their response is stored in the cache. Using Burp, you can then send a request to the same URL to fetch the cached response containing the victim\'s data. Avoid doing this directly in the browser as some applications redirect users without a session or invalidate local data, which could hide a vulnerability.' => 'Susun URL jebakan agar cache menyimpan respons korban saat korban mengunjunginya, lalu ambil salinan dari cache tanpa sesi melalui klien HTTP terpisah.',
    "We'll explore some different approaches for constructing a web cache deception attack." => 'Berikut beberapa pendekatan eksploitasi secara rinci.',
    'Using a cache buster' => 'Menggunakan cache buster',
    'While testing for discrepancies and crafting a web cache deception exploit, make sure that each request you send has a different cache key. Otherwise, you may be served cached responses, which will impact your test results.' => 'Pastikan tiap permintaan uji memakai cache key unik agar tidak tertipu hasil cache lama.',
    "As both URL path and any query parameters are typically included in the cache key, you can change the key by adding a query string to the path and changing it each time you send a request. Automate this process using the Param Miner extension. To do this, once you've installed the extension, click on the top-level <strong>Param miner &gt; Settings</strong> menu, then select <strong>Add dynamic cachebuster</strong>. Burp now adds a unique query string to every request that you make. You can view the added query strings in the <strong>Logger</strong> tab." => 'Tambahkan parameter query acak yang selalu berubah pada setiap pengujian agar cache buster memicu pengambilan baru.',
    'Detecting cached responses' => 'Mendeteksi respons yang di-cache',
