    'Discrepancies in how the cache and origin server map the URL path to resources can result in web cache deception vulnerabilities. Consider the following example:' => 'Selisih antara server asal (REST) dan cache (tradisional) menimbulkan celah pada contoh berikut:',
    'An origin server using REST-style URL mapping may interpret this as a request for the [[C0]] endpoint and returns the profile information for user [[C1]], ignoring [[C2]] as a non-significant parameter.' => 'Server asal hanya melihat endpoint [[C0]] milik pengguna [[C1]] dan mengabaikan akhiran [[C2]].',
    'A cache that uses traditional URL mapping may view this as a request for a file named [[C0]] located in the [[C1]] directory under [[C2]]. It interprets the URL path as [[C3]]. If the cache is configured to store responses for requests where the path ends in [[C4]], it would cache and serve the profile information as if it were a CSS file.' => 'Cache mengira [[C3]] sebagai file [[C0]] di dalam [[C1]] di bawah [[C2]] dan menyimpannya karena berakhiran [[C4]].',
    'Exploiting path mapping discrepancies' => 'Mengeksploitasi perbedaan pemetaan path',
    'To test how the origin server maps the URL path to resources, add an arbitrary path segment to the URL of your target endpoint. If the response still contains the same sensitive data as the base response, it indicates that the origin server abstracts the URL path and ignores the added segment. For example, this is the case if modifying [[C0]] to [[C1]] still returns order information.' => 'Tambahkan segmen acak setelah path endpoint (misalnya [[C0]] menjadi [[C1]]) untuk melihat apakah server asal tetap mengembalikan data sensitif.',
