    "The cache also uses the [[C0]] character as a delimiter, but doesn't decode [[C1]]. It interprets the path as [[C2]]. If there is a cache rule for the [[C3]] extension it will store the response." => 'Cache tidak mendekode [[C1]] saat membaca [[C0]] sehingga tetap melihat [[C2]] dan menyimpannya karena berakhiran [[C3]].',
    'In addition, some cache servers may decode the URL and then forward the request with the decoded characters. Others first apply cache rules based on the encoded URL, then decode the URL and forward it to the next server. These behaviors can also result in discrepancies in the way cache and origin server interpret the URL path. Consider the example [[C0]]:' => 'Sebaliknya pada [[C0]], cache mengevaluasi aturan sebelum meneruskan versi terdekode:',
    'The cache server applies the cache rules based on the encoded path [[C0]] and decides to store the response as there is a cache rule for the [[C1]] extension. It then decodes [[C2]] to [[C3]] and forwards the rewritten request to the origin server.' => 'Cache mencocokkan aturan [[C1]] terhadap [[C0]], lalu mendekode [[C2]] ke [[C3]] saat meneruskannya ke server asal.',
    'The origin server receives the request [[C0]]. It uses the [[C1]] character as a delimiter, so it interprets the path as [[C2]].' => 'Server asal menerima [[C0]], memotong pada [[C1]], dan mengembalikan [[C2]].',
    'Exploiting delimiter decoding discrepancies' => 'Mengeksploitasi perbedaan dekode delimiter',
