    'Exploiting static directory cache rules' => 'Mengeksploitasi aturan cache direktori statis',
    "It's common practice for web servers to store static resources in specific directories. Cache rules often target these directories by matching specific URL path prefixes, like [[C0]], [[C1]], [[C2]], or [[C3]]. These rules can also be vulnerable to web cache deception." => 'Cache sering menyimpan semua respons di bawah prefiks direktori seperti [[C0]], [[C1]], [[C2]], atau [[C3]].',
    "To exploit static directory cache rules, you'll need to understand the basics of path traversal attacks. For more information, see our [[A0]]Path traversal[[/A0]] Academy topic." => 'Eksploitasi aturan direktori statis memerlukan teknik dasar [[A0]]Path traversal[[/A0]].',
    'Normalization discrepancies' => 'Perbedaan normalisasi path',
    'Normalization involves converting various representations of URL paths into a standardized format. This sometimes includes decoding encoded characters and resolving dot-segments, but this varies significantly from parser to parser.' => 'Normalisasi path melibatkan dekode karakter ter-encode dan penyelesaian segmen titik relatif (dot-segments), yang sering berbeda antar-parser.',
    'Discrepancies in how the cache and origin server normalize the URL can enable an attacker to construct a path traversal payload that is interpreted differently by each parser. Consider the example [[C0]]:' => 'Contoh perbedaan normalisasi path pada URL [[C0]]:',
    'An origin server that decodes slash characters and resolves dot-segments would normalize the path to [[C0]] and return profile information.' => 'Server asal mendekode garis miring dan menyelesaikan traversal sehingga melayani [[C0]].',
    "A cache that doesn't resolve dot-segments or decode slashes would interpret the path as [[C0]]. If the cache stores responses for requests with the [[C1]] prefix, it would cache and serve the profile information." => 'Cache yang tidak menormalisasi tetap melihat prefiks [[C1]] pada [[C0]] dan menyimpan responsnya.',
    "As shown in the above example, each dot-segment in the path traversal sequence needs to be encoded. Otherwise, the victim's browser will resolve it before forwarding the request to the cache. Therefore, an exploitable normalization discrepancy requires that either the cache or origin server decodes characters in the path traversal sequence as well as resolving dot-segments." => 'Bagian traversal harus di-URL-encode agar tidak diselesaikan lebih dulu oleh browser korban sebelum keluar.',
    'Detecting normalization by the origin server' => 'Mendeteksi normalisasi oleh server asal',
    'To test how the origin server normalizes the URL path, send a request to a non-cacheable resource with a path traversal sequence and an arbitrary directory at the start of the path. To choose a non-cacheable resource, look for a non-idempotent method like [[C0]]. For example, modify [[C1]] to [[C2]]:' => 'Kirim permintaan yang tidak di-cache (misal metode [[C0]]) dengan traversal ter-encode dari [[C1]] menjadi [[C2]]:',
    'If the response matches the base response and returns the profile information, this indicates that the path has been interpreted as [[C0]]. The origin server decodes the slash and resolves the dot-segment.' => 'Jika respons identik dengan halaman asli, server asal berhasil menormalisasi menjadi [[C0]].',
    "If the response doesn't match the base response, for example returning a [[C0]] error message, this indicates that the path has been interpreted as [[C1]]. The origin server either doesn't decode the slash or resolve the dot-segment." => 'Jika mengembalikan [[C0]] untuk [[C1]], server asal tidak menormalisasi urutan tersebut.',
    'When testing for normalization, start by encoding only the second slash in the dot-segment. This is important because some CDNs match the slash following the static directory prefix.' => 'Awali dengan meng-encode garis miring kedua saja agar pencocokan prefiks direktori statis di CDN tetap utuh.',
    'You can also try encoding the full path traversal sequence, or encoding a dot instead of the slash. This can sometimes impact whether the parser decodes the sequence.' => 'Anda juga dapat mencoba meng-encode seluruh rangkaian traversal atau tanda titiknya.',
    'Detecting normalization by the cache server' => 'Mendeteksi normalisasi oleh server cache',
    'You can use a few different methods to test how the cache normalizes the path. Start by identifying potential static directories. In <strong>Proxy &gt; HTTP history</strong>, look for requests with common static directory prefixes and cached responses. Focus on static resources by setting the HTTP history filter to only show messages with 2xx responses and script, images, and CSS MIME types.' => 'Temukan direktori statis yang di-cache lewat riwayat HTTP (respons 2xx untuk skrip, gambar, atau CSS).',
    'You can then choose a request with a cached response and resend the request with a path traversal sequence and an arbitrary directory at the start of the static path. Choose a request with a response that contains evidence of being cached. For example, [[C0]]:' => 'Uji apakah prefiks traversal sebelumnya (seperti [[C0]]) tetap menghasilkan cache hit:',
    "If the response is no longer cached, this indicates that the cache isn't normalizing the path before mapping it to the endpoint. It shows that there is a cache rule based on the [[C0]] prefix." => 'Jika tak lagi ter-cache, berarti cache tidak menormalisasi path dan memang ada aturan prefiks [[C0]].',
    'If the response is still cached, this may indicate that the cache has normalized the path to [[C0]].' => 'Jika masih ter-cache, cache mungkin telah menormalisasinya ke [[C0]].',
    'You can also add a path traversal sequence after the directory prefix. For example, modify [[C0]] to [[C1]]:' => 'Coba pula menyisipkan traversal tepat sesudah prefiks statis, dari [[C0]] ke [[C1]]:',
    'If the response is no longer cached, this indicates that the cache decodes the slash and resolves the dot-segment during normalization, interpreting the path as [[C0]]. It shows that there is a cache rule based on the [[C1]] prefix.' => 'Jika tak lagi di-cache, cache telah menormalisasinya keluar dari [[C1]] menjadi [[C0]].',
    "If the response is still cached, this may indicate that the cache hasn't decoded the slash or resolved the dot-segment, interpreting the path as [[C0]]." => 'Jika tetap di-cache, cache membiarkan [[C0]] tanpa dekode/resolusi.',
    "Note that in both cases, the response may be cached due to another cache rule, such as one based on the file extension. To confirm that the cache rule is based on the static directory, replace the path after the directory prefix with an arbitrary string. For example, [[C0]]. If the response is still cached, this confirms the cache rule is based on the [[C1]] prefix. Note that if the response doesn't appear to be cached, this doesn't necessarily rule out a static directory cache rule as sometimes [[C2]] responses aren't cached." => 'Pastikan caching memang dipicu prefiks [[C1]] (bukan ekstensi file) dengan menguji [[C0]], dengan catatan respons [[C2]] kadang tidak disimpan.',
    "It's possible that you may not be able to definitively determine whether the cache decodes dot-segments and decodes the URL path without attempting an exploit." => 'Terkadang kepastian penuh baru tampak saat langsung menguji rantai eksploitasi.',
    'Exploiting normalization by the origin server' => 'Mengeksploitasi normalisasi oleh server asal',
    "If the origin server resolves encoded dot-segments, but the cache doesn't, you can attempt to exploit the discrepancy by constructing a payload according to the following structure:" => 'Jika hanya server asal yang menormalisasi traversal ter-encode, susun payload dengan pola:',
    'For example, consider the payload [[C0]]:' => 'Contohnya pada payload [[C0]]:',
    'The cache interprets the path as: [[C0]]' => 'Cache membaca path sebagai: [[C0]]',
    'The origin server interprets the path as: [[C0]]' => 'Server asal membaca path sebagai: [[C0]]',
    'Exploiting normalization by the cache server' => 'Mengeksploitasi normalisasi oleh server cache',
    'If the cache server resolves encoded dot-segments but the origin server doesn\'t, you can attempt to exploit the discrepancy by constructing a payload according to the following structure:' => 'Jika hanya server cache yang menormalisasi segmen titik ter-encode, gunakan pola berikut:',
    "When exploiting normalization by the cache server, encode all characters in the path traversal sequence. Using encoded characters helps avoid unexpected behavior when using delimiters, and there's no need to have an unencoded slash following the static directory prefix since the cache will handle the decoding." => 'Encode seluruh karakter traversal (titik dan kedua garis miring) agar tidak terbentur aturan delimiter server asal.',
    "In this situation, path traversal alone isn't sufficient for an exploit. For example, consider how the cache and origin server interpret the payload [[C0]]:" => 'Traversal saja belum cukup bila server asal tetap mendapat path lengkap seperti [[C0]]:',
    'The origin server is likely to return an error message instead of profile information.' => 'Server asal biasanya membalas pesan galat alih-alih data profil.',
    "To exploit this discrepancy, you'll need to also identify a delimiter that is used by the origin server but not the cache. Test possible delimiters by adding them to the payload after the dynamic path:" => 'Tambahkan delimiter yang hanya dipahami server asal tepat setelah path dinamis target:',
    'If the origin server uses a delimiter, it will truncate the URL path and return the dynamic information.' => 'Server asal memotong sisa traversal setelah delimiter dan mengembalikan data dinamis.',
    "If the cache doesn't use the delimiter, it will resolve the path and cache the response." => 'Cache mengabaikan delimiter tersebut, menyelesaikan traversal ke folder statis, lalu menyimpan responsnya.',
    'For example, consider the payload [[C0]]. The origin server uses [[C1]] as a delimiter:' => 'Misalnya pada [[C0]] ketika server asal memakai [[C1]] sebagai delimiter:',
    'The origin server returns the dynamic profile information, which is stored in the cache. You can therefore use this payload for an exploit.' => 'Respons profil dinamis korban langsung tersimpan di entri cache folder statis.',

    // File name rules & prevention
    'Exploiting file name cache rules' => 'Mengeksploitasi aturan cache nama file',
    'Certain files such as [[C0]], [[C1]], and [[C2]] are common files found on web servers. They\'re often cached due to their infrequent changes. Cache rules target these files by matching the exact file name string.' => 'Berkas standar seperti [[C0]], [[C1]], dan [[C2]] sering di-cache berdasarkan kecocokan nama file persis.',
    'To identify whether there is a file name cache rule, send a [[C0]] request for a possible file and see if the response is cached.' => 'Kirim permintaan [[C0]] ke kandidat nama berkas tersebut untuk mengecek apakah responsnya disimpan di cache.',
    'Detecting normalization discrepancies' => 'Mendeteksi perbedaan normalisasi',
    'To test how the origin server normalizes the URL path, use the same method that you used for static directory cache rules. For more information, see [[A0]]Detecting normalization by the origin server[[/A0]].' => 'Uji normalisasi server asal memakai metode [[A0]]mendeteksi normalisasi server asal[[/A0]] seperti sebelumnya.',
    'To test how the cache normalizes the URL path, send a request with a path traversal sequence and an arbitrary directory before the file name. For example, [[C0]]:' => 'Lalu uji normalisasi cache dengan menyisipkan direktori acak dan traversal sebelum nama file, seperti [[C0]]:',
    'If the response is cached, this indicates that the cache normalizes the path to [[C0]].' => 'Jika ter-cache, berarti cache telah menormalisasinya menjadi [[C0]].',
    "If the response isn't cached, this indicates that the cache doesn't decode the slash and resolve the dot-segment, interpreting the path as [[C0]]." => 'Jika tidak ter-cache, cache membiarkan [[C0]] apa adanya.',
    'Exploiting normalization discrepancies' => 'Mengeksploitasi perbedaan normalisasi',
    "Because the response is only cached if the request matches the exact file name, you can only exploit a discrepancy where the cache server resolves encoded dot-segments, but the origin server doesn't. Use the same method as for static directory cache rules - simply replace the static directory prefix with the file name. For more information, see [[A0]]Exploiting normalization by the cache server[[/A0]]." => 'Gabungkan traversal ter-encode menuju nama berkas dengan delimiter server asal sebagaimana dijelaskan pada [[A0]]eksploitasi normalisasi oleh server cache[[/A0]].',
    'Preventing web cache deception vulnerabilities' => 'Mencegah kerentanan web cache deception',
    'You can take a range of steps to prevent web cache deception vulnerabilities:' => 'Langkah-langkah pencegahan web cache deception:',
    'Always use [[C0]] headers to mark dynamic resources, set with the directives [[C1]] and [[C2]].' => 'Selalu pasang header [[C0]] berisi direktif [[C1]] dan [[C2]] pada seluruh respons dinamis/sensitif.',
    "Configure your CDN settings so that your caching rules don't override the [[C0]] header." => 'Pastikan aturan CDN tidak mengabaikan header [[C0]] dari server asal.',
    "Activate any protection that your CDN has against web cache deception attacks. Many CDNs enable you to set a cache rule that verifies that the response [[C0]] matches the request's URL file extension. For example, Cloudflare's Cache Deception Armor." => 'Aktifkan validasi kesesuaian [[C0]] respons dengan ekstensi file pada URL di konfigurasi CDN Anda.',
    "Verify that there aren't any discrepancies between how the origin server and the cache interpret URL paths." => 'Selaraskan aturan normalisasi path dan delimiter antara proxy cache dan server aplikasi.',
];
